  "question": {
    "text": "If a magnet is plugged into a coil, then the magnitude of induced emf does not depend upon"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The number of turns in the coil",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The medium of the core of the coil",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The strength of the magnet",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The resistance of the coil",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The magnitude of induced emf is given by, <math><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Which depends upon the number of turns (N), magnetic field intensity (B) which depends upon the medium, rate of change of area <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> which depends upon insertion speed of magnet. It is independent of resistance of the coil."
  }
}